{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4359356","formula":"ClNO₅","hill":"ClNO5","elements":["N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"N":1.0,"O":5.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Nitrosyl perchlorate","ru":"Перхлорат нитрозила"},"descriptions":{"en":"Nitrosyl perchlorate or nitrosonium perchlorate is the inorganic compound with the formula NO(ClO4). A hygroscopic white solid, it is the salt of the nitrosonium cation with the perchlorate anion. It is an oxidant and strong electrophile, but has fallen out of use with the availability of the closely related salt nitrosonium tetrafluoroborate NO(BF4).","ru":"Перхлорат нитрозила — неорганическое соединение, соль нитрозила и хлорной кислоты с формулой NOClO4, бесцветные кристаллы, образует кристаллогидрат."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":177613,"mass":129.46,"charge":0,"smiles":"N(=O)OCl(=O)(=O)=O","inchikey":"ONKVXKHGDFDPFZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"perchloryl nitrite","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"177613","atoms":7,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.611,"y":0.169,"z":-0.478,"el":"N"},{"x":2.781,"y":0.17,"z":-0.075,"el":"O"},{"x":0.697,"y":-0.058,"z":0.598,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.914,"y":-0.067,"z":0.091,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.769,"y":-0.303,"z":1.241,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.27,"y":1.211,"z":-0.498,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.137,"y":-1.124,"z":-0.879,"el":"O"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2.0],[0,2,1.0],[2,3,1.0],[3,4,1.0],[3,5,1.0],[3,6,1.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4359356","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitrosyl_perchlorate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%85%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82_%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D